# QA Result

> Read a person's QA round (a Claude Docs doc from `battoni-new-qa-session`), check every problem
> against the app before calling it a bug, and turn each one into the right next step. Works days
> later, in a fresh session, after the merge or before it: everything it needs is found from the
> link, never from memory of the session that wrote the doc.
>
> **Usage:** `/battoni-qa-result <doc link>` — from the monorepo root. Pass the link, never pasted
> text: a paste loses the result chips, the comments and the way to fix a step in place.
> Reads with the `battoni-new-qa-session` skill, mode **recolher** (load it); this command adds what
> a feature needs around it.

## Step 1 — Find the feature (from the link alone)

1. **Doc id** = the end of the link. `rtk git fetch -q origin`, then look for it in every feature's
   `state.md` → `## QA`: on `main` (`grep -l <id> specs/*/state.md`) and on every open feature branch
   (`git show <branch>:specs/<id>-*/state.md`). The doc's line there names the round, the tester and
   the env. `/battoni-verify` writes that line when it makes the doc, and so does the skill when the
   doc is made outside verify, so the doc always has a home.
2. **Not found** → the doc belongs to no feature (an ad-hoc round on the whole product): ask the
   owner once which PRs it covers, then follow the skill's recolher mode alone and stop.
3. **Where the code is now:** `gh pr list --state all --head <branch>` for the feature's PR.

| PR state | A real bug is fixed… | Where the record goes |
| --- | --- | --- |
| open (draft or not) | on the feature branch, in its worktree (`EnterWorktree` with `path: .claude/worktrees/<id>`; none → `rtk make wt-new ID=<id> BRANCH=<branch>` first), never a checkout in the main checkout | the branch's `state.md` |
| merged | through the **small track**: a new ID, its own `fix/` branch and PR, citing the `R#` it broke (`.claude/feature-flow.md`, "After delivery") | `state.md` on `main`, through that fix PR |
| closed, not merged | nowhere until the owner says: ask | — |

A worktree the sweep removed is no loss: the branch is on GitHub
(`rtk make wt-new ID=<id> BRANCH=<branch>` brings it back, with its deps; the browser
stack is `make fresh-seed` plus `make serve-api`/`make serve-app` from it, when a step needs it), and a merged feature lives on `main`. A small-track fix gets its
own: `rtk make wt-new ID=<new id> BRANCH=fix/<new id>-<slug>`.

## Step 2 — Read only the new answers

- Spawn one `battoni-reader` (Haiku) or `general-purpose` agent with `model: sonnet` to read the doc
  (skill, recolher steps 1–3) and return **only**: each row that is not "Funcionou" (step number,
  its `A#`, the Observação), the rows still unanswered, the comments, and the filled lines of the
  problem log. The main session never reads the whole doc: a round of 85 steps is ~60k of XML.
- **A round in parts.** The doc's `## QA` line in `state.md` ends with `collected: rev <n>` after
  each run. On the next run, ask the reader for changes since that rev (`sinceRev`), so a tester who
  takes days is collected as often as wanted, and only what changed is judged again.
- The tester may still be at work: a step without an answer is "not run yet", never a failure.

## Step 3 — Check each problem before it is a bug

The app may have moved since the doc was written (later PRs). Judge on the code that is live for the
tester: the PR's branch when it is open, `main` when it is merged.

1. **Re-run the step** where it can be run without the person: the local API through `tinker` or
   Pest, or one `battoni-chrome-driver` round for a screen. In boanerges-3, 10.6 "the banner stays"
   reproduced as working: the step pointed at the wrong week, so it was the script's fault.
2. Then sort it, as the skill says:
   - **script error** (wrong label, wrong week, wrong expectation) → fix the step's text in the doc
     and in `qa-script.md`; never the tester's answer, chip or note;
   - **environment** (old `main`, seeder not run, missing login) → one line for the tester;
   - **violates an A#** → a bug: a failing test first, then the fix, in the place the table above
     says;
   - **outside the spec** → a new D# or a new intent, the owner's call; never fixed in silence.

Ask the owner (one `AskUserQuestion`) only for what the sort cannot settle: a bug that needs a
product decision, an "outside the spec", a PR that was closed.

## Step 4 — Record and close the loop

- The doc: the skill's round summary at the top ("Rodada N concluída em …").
- `state.md` → `## QA`, on the doc's line: `collected: rev <n> · <date> · <x> passed, <y> problems
  (<IDs opened>), <z> not run`. Committed with the fix it records, or alone (`<id>: Record the QA
  round`) on the branch, or through the small-track PR when the feature is merged.
- **Merge gate.** When `plan.md` → `## QA` says the merge waits for this round: every step answered
  and no open bug → `state.md` Next = "merge", and say the draft PR can be marked ready; otherwise
  Next names what is still owed.
- A round that is not finished is recorded too (`<z> not run`), so the next session sees it.

## Step 5 — Report

One screen: the counts, each real bug (step, `A#`, where it is fixed and its ID), the script steps
corrected, the environment notes, what is still unanswered. Then a message for the tester, in
pt-BR, one paragraph per line, ready to paste: what changed in the doc and which steps to redo.
